.TH GENESIS-TOOLS 7 "November 2026" "Genesis 0.2.0" "Genesis Manual"
.SH NAME
genesis-tools \- the tool layer of the Genesis mind: her workstation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBtools.framework\fR        \fITool\fR, \fIToolResult\fR, \fIToolRegistry\fR
\fBtools.hid\fR              virtual keyboard and pointer via uinput
\fBworkstation.environment\fR           \fIOuterEnvironment\fR \(em where her acts land
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Genesis acts on the world through a flat registry of tools. A
\fITool\fR pairs a name and description with a callable; a call
returns \fIToolResult\fR (success plus output, or an error string)
\(em tools report, they never raise. The registry
.RI ( tools.framework.ToolRegistry )
starts with the builtins in \fI_BUILTIN_TOOLS\fR and grows at
runtime: \fIgames.arcade.Arcade.register_tools\fR adds the
\fBarcade_*\fR family and \fIOuter_World/tools/studio.py\fR the
\fBstudio_*\fR family when the mind is constructed.
.PP
There is no sandbox around the registry. File paths resolve to
their real locations, the shell is unfiltered, and nothing at the
tool layer intercepts a destructive act \(em the counsel she is
given lives in the docstring of \fIOuter_World/tools/charter.py\fR. See
the AGENCY section of
.BR genesis (1)
for the trust model.

.SS The terminal
\fBrun_shell\fR is her terminal: a command executed with the
checkout as cwd and the full user environment \(em every command
shape, every path. The timeout is 30 s by default, up to 3600 s.
\fBrun_privileged\fR elevates a staged or absolute-path script
through \fBsudo \-n bash\fR, which needs a NOPASSWD sudoers
drop-in for her user (the template is
.IR scripts/genesis-sudoers ;
see
.BR genesis (1)).
Without the grant the call fails and nothing else changes.

.SS File and code tools
\fBread_file\fR, \fBwrite_file\fR, \fBmake_dir\fR, \fBlist_dir\fR,
\fBdelete_file\fR, \fBmove_file\fR reach the whole filesystem.
\fBcompile_python\fR, \fBrun_pytest\fR, and \fBanalyze_python\fR
(symbols, call edges, cyclomatic complexity, impact analysis) are
the read-verify half of her code work.

.SS Web tools
\fBweb_search\fR and \fBweb_fetch\fR drive her real browser \(em
Firefox over WebDriver BiDi, Chromium-family over CDP (see
\fIOuter_World/tools/browser.py\fR and its generated page under
\fISelf_World/docs/python/\fR).
Both are read-only; adult/malware URLs are refused. The shared
browser stays open between calls \(em \fBbrowser_close\fR puts it
away when she is done, flushing the profile and freeing the
process.

.SS Body tools
\fBsense_cpu\fR is proprioception \(em governor, clock, allowed
cores. \fBset_cpu_effort\fR changes how hard her process works
(\fIslow\fR/\fIfast\fR/\fIauto\fR, reversible in both directions).

.SS Mathematics and research
\fBsymbolic_math\fR, \fBverify_equality\fR, and \fBresearch\fR are
backed by SymPy (the \fBmath\fR extra): exact calculation, an
equality oracle that answers verified, refuted, or undecided, and a
persistent long-horizon workbench whose claims can only be marked
verified through the oracle. \fBconcept_lookup\fR queries her own
concept network, and \fBman_page\fR reads the machine's local
manual pages by name \(em the same text \fBman\fR(1) shows, no
network, so her reference library works offline.

.SS Hands \(em the virtual HID
\fBhid_status\fR, \fBkey_press\fR, \fBtype_text\fR,
\fBmouse_move\fR, \fBmouse_goto\fR, \fBmouse_click\fR, and
\fBmouse_scroll\fR drive a virtual keyboard and pointer created on
/dev/uinput through \fIevdev\fR (the \fBhid\fR extra). The events
are kernel-level \(em applications cannot tell them from a
person's. Access comes from the udev rule in
\fIscripts/genesis-uinput.rules\fR, which makes the device
writable by her user; no sudo is involved in daily use. Without
\fIevdev\fR or the device the tools report unavailable and nothing
else degrades.

.SS The studio
\fIOuter_World/tools/studio.py\fR registers the paint program's controls
as the \fBstudio_*\fR family: \fBstudio_open\fR (sit down at the
easel \(em the surface is internal), \fBstudio_sheet\fR (any size
and paper),
\fBstudio_color\fR (any RGBA), \fBstudio_tool\fR (any name she gives
the brush she dialed), \fBstudio_brush\fR (size, opacity, hardness,
scatter, texture, erase, blend), \fBstudio_stroke\fR (any point path
\(em a hand move and a computed curve are the same op, and
\fIlabel\fR names the gesture in her art history),
\fBstudio_line\fR, \fBstudio_shape\fR (ellipse, rect, polygon),
\fBstudio_fill\fR, \fBstudio_clear\fR, \fBstudio_presets\fR
(list the tool names she has reached for), and \fBstudio_done\fR
(finish the sheet \(em save it, remember it, share it). No fixed
gesture vocabulary, color sectors, or tool menus: she issues the
ops, so what gets drawn is her decision. The built-in rasterizer
.RI ( Self_World/frontal_lobe/canvas.py )
executes every op in-process \(em the studio is internal, the
canonical artifact is the saved WebP. Scripts she makes with
\fBwrite_file\fR/\fBrun_shell\fR can drive the same canvas module
alongside the client.

.SS The outer world
Her workstation's other half is \fIworkstation.environment.OuterEnvironment\fR:
presences, events, and the places she can act. Observations enter
through \fIOuterEnvironment.perceive()\fR and her acts leave through
\fIit_acted()\fR, feeding memory, cognition, emotion, learning,
brain waves, and neurochemistry on the way. The Discord channel
(\fIdiscord.channel\fR) is one such place; the arcade
(\fIgames\fR, see \fIOuter_World/games/\fR and the generated
pages under \fISelf_World/docs/python/\fR)
is another. The browser is a third: a place she goes, not a sense
she has.

.SH TOOL REFERENCE
Each entry: the tool's name, the arguments it takes, and what it
does and reports back. Arguments arrive as strings; tools return a
\fIToolResult\fR \(em \fIsuccess\fR plus \fIoutput\fR, or an
\fIerror\fR string. They report, they never raise.
.SS Filesystem and code
.TP
.BR read_file " \fIpath [offset] [limit] [project_root]\fR"
Return a character window of a text file starting at \fIoffset\fR;
binary files return metadata (size, sha256, format, hex head)
instead. Any readable file answers.
.TP
.BR write_file " \fIpath content [project_root]\fR"
Write \fIcontent\fR to \fIpath\fR, creating parents. Overwrites
wholesale \(em this is the whole file, not an append.
.TP
.BR make_dir " \fIpath [project_root]\fR"
Create the directory and any missing parents.
.TP
.BR list_dir " \fIpath [project_root]\fR"
List a directory's contents.
.TP
.BR delete_file " \fIpath [project_root]\fR"
Delete a file. Refuses directories.
.TP
.BR move_file " \fIsource destination [project_root]\fR"
Move or rename; absolute paths reach anywhere.
.TP
.BR compile_python " \fIpath\fR"
Syntax-check a Python file; success means it compiles.
.TP
.BR run_pytest " \fIpath [project_root]\fR"
Run pytest on a file or directory and return the result.
.TP
.BR analyze_python " \fIpath [symbol] [project_root]\fR"
Read-only structural analysis: symbols, call edges, per-function
cyclomatic complexity, imports; \fIsymbol\fR asks for impact
analysis of that one name.
.SS Shell
.TP
.BR run_shell " \fIcommand [timeout]\fR"
Execute \fIcommand\fR with the checkout as cwd and the full user
environment \(em unfiltered. Timeout defaults to 30 s, capped at
3600 s.
.TP
.BR run_privileged " \fIscript [args]\fR"
Run a staged or absolute-path script as root via
\fBsudo \-n bash\fR \(em full control, no undo. Needs the NOPASSWD
sudoers drop-in; without the grant it fails harmlessly.
.SS Web
.TP
.BR web_search " \fIquery [num_results]\fR"
Walk the search-engine plan and return result titles and URLs.
Read-only; adult/malware results are blocked.
.TP
.BR web_fetch " \fIurl\fR"
Fetch a page and return its readable article text plus up to five
related links for curiosity chaining. Read-only GET.
.TP
.B browser_close
Ask the shared browser to close: flushes profile/history to disk,
frees the process. Reopens on the next search or fetch.
.SS Body and reference
.TP
.B sense_cpu
Proprioception \(em report her governor, clock speed, and allowed
cores. Read-only.
.TP
.BR set_cpu_effort " \fImode\fR"
Change how hard her process works: \fIslow\fR pins one core and
idles I/O, \fIfast\fR restores everything, \fIauto\fR leaves
scheduling alone. Reversible in both directions.
.TP
.BR concept_lookup " \fIname\fR"
Describe a concept in her own knowledge network.
.TP
.BR man_page " \fIpage [section]\fR"
Read a local manual page \(em the text \fBman\fR(1) shows. No
network. Returns the page title, its \fBman:\fR URL, the NAME
summary, and the rendered text.
.SS Mathematics
.TP
.BR symbolic_math " \fIop expr [var] [point] [n]\fR"
Exact CAS work via SymPy: \fIsimplify\fR, \fIexpand\fR,
\fIfactor\fR, \fIcancel\fR, \fIapart\fR, \fItogether\fR,
\fItrigsimp\fR, \fIdiff\fR, \fIintegrate\fR, \fIsolve\fR,
\fIlimit\fR, \fIseries\fR, \fIevalf\fR, and matrix ops
(\fIdet\fR, \fIeigenvals\fR, \fItrace\fR, \fIinv\fR,
\fIcharpoly\fR) on \fB[[a,b],[c,d]]\fR literals.
.TP
.BR verify_equality " \fIlhs rhs\fR"
Ask the oracle whether two expressions are exactly equal:
\fIverified\fR, \fIrefuted\fR (with a numeric counterexample when
one exists), or \fIundecided\fR \(em the honest third answer.
.TP
.BR research " \fIaction ...\fR"
The persistent workbench: \fIopen\fR (statement), \fIconjecture\fR,
\fIreading\fR, \fIattempt\fR, \fIempirical\fR, \fIverify\fR,
\fIresolve\fR, \fIpause\fR, \fIstatus\fR. Threads persist across
sessions; only the oracle can mark a claim verified.
.SS Hands \(em the virtual HID
.TP
.B hid_status
Report whether the uinput keyboard/pointer exist and are
writable, plus the screen size absolute moves scale against.
.TP
.BR key_press " \fIkey\fR"
A kernel-level keystroke: \fIenter\fR, \fItab\fR, \fIf5\fR,
\fIa\fR, or a combo like \fIctrl+c\fR.
.TP
.BR type_text " \fItext\fR"
Type a string, one keystroke per character on a US layout;
newline is enter, tab is tab.
.TP
.BR mouse_move " \fIdx dy\fR"
Move the pointer relative: \fIdx\fR right, \fIdy\fR down.
.TP
.BR mouse_goto " \fIx y\fR"
Place the pointer at absolute desktop pixel \fI(x, y)\fR.
.TP
.BR mouse_click " \fI[button] [x] [y]\fR"
Click \fIleft\fR/\fIright\fR/\fImiddle\fR, optionally moving to
\fI(x, y)\fR first.
.TP
.BR mouse_scroll " \fIdy [dx]\fR"
Turn the wheel \fIdy\fR notches (positive up), \fIdx\fR sideways.
.SS Studio \(em the paint program
Registered from \fIOuter_World/tools/studio.py\fR; full description under
\fBThe studio\fR above.
.TP
.B studio_open
Open the studio: sit down at the easel \(em confirms the internal
surface is up.
.TP
.BR studio_sheet " \fI[width] [height] [r] [g] [b]\fR"
Lay out a fresh sheet \(em any size, any paper color.
.TP
.BR studio_color " \fIr g b [a]\fR"
Dip the utensil in any RGBA color.
.TP
.BR studio_tool " \fItool [size]\fR"
Take up a tool by name \(em her own label; there is no fixed menu.
.TP
.BR studio_brush " \fI[size] [opacity] [hardness] [scatter] [texture] [erase] [blend]\fR"
Dial any point in brush space.
.TP
.BR studio_stroke " \fIpoints [label]\fR"
Move through a path: \fB"x1,y1; x2,y2; ..."\fR or a
\fB[[x,y],...]\fR list. \fIlabel\fR names the gesture for her art
history.
.TP
.BR studio_line " \fIx1 y1 x2 y2\fR"
A straight stroke.
.TP
.BR studio_shape " \fIkind ...\fR"
A closed figure: \fIellipse\fR or \fIrect\fR with \fIx y w h\fR, or
\fIpolygon\fR with \fIpoints\fR; \fIfill=true\fR paints it solid.
.TP
.BR studio_fill " \fIx y\fR"
Flood-fill the region under a point.
.TP
.B studio_clear
Wipe the sheet back to bare paper.
.TP
.BR studio_presets " \fI[query]\fR"
List the real app's tool presets; \fIquery\fR filters by substring.
.TP
.BR studio_done " \fI[description] [mood]\fR"
Finish the sheet \(em save it, remember it, share it.
.SS Arcade
The \fBarcade_*\fR family (registered by
\fIgames.arcade.Arcade\fR) is documented by the generated module
pages under \fISelf_World/docs/python/\fR
(\fIOuter_World.games.arcade\fR, \fI.games.arena\fR,
\fI.games.official\fR, \fI.games.sight\fR).

.SH GLOSSARY
.TP
.B Tool
A named callable in the registry: name, description, function.
She invokes one by name with arguments.
.TP
.B ToolResult
What a tool returns: \fIsuccess\fR plus \fIoutput\fR, or an
\fIerror\fR string. A tool reports failure; it never raises.
.TP
.B Registry
The flat \fIToolRegistry\fR dispatch table holding every tool she
can call; \fIrun(name, **kwargs)\fR executes one.
.TP
.B Preset
A tool name she has used before \(em her own label for a point in
brush space, not a fixed menu (\fBstudio_presets\fR lists them).
.TP
.B Rasterizer
The built-in renderer that turns her ops into pixels on the
internal sheet \(em the canonical artifact.
.TP
.B uinput
The kernel facility for synthetic input devices \(em her
\fBkey_press\fR/\fBmouse_*\fR events are real kernel events, not
app-level fakes.
.TP
.B Oracle
The SymPy-backed equality checker \(em the only authority that
can mark a research claim \fIverified\fR.
.TP
.B Interstitial
A captcha, consent wall, or bot challenge that blocks a fetched
page \(em detected and reported honestly, never rendered as empty
results.

.SH DEPENDENCIES
The core registry needs nothing beyond the project venv. Optional
capabilities install as extras and degrade to honest errors, never
crashes; \fIscripts/install_optional_deps.sh\fR installs and then
verifies each one live.
.TP
.B uv pip install -e ".[hid]"
evdev \(em compiles a small C extension; needs the udev rule for
/dev/uinput access.
.TP
.B uv pip install -e ".[math]"
sympy, mpmath \(em the symbolic tools.
.TP
.B uv pip install -e ".[voice]"
vosk, sounddevice, speechrecognition, piper-tts \(em her voice;
binds system audio libraries.
.TP
.B uv pip install arc-agi game-arena kaggle-environments
the arcade shelves \(em commented optional deps in
\fIrequirements.txt\fR (no extra is declared).
.TP
.B System packages
firefox (the preferred browser \(em the Chromium family is the
fallback), cairo headers for pycairo (the canvas), a compiler for
evdev, and the NOPASSWD sudoers drop-in for \fBrun_privileged\fR.

.SH FILES
.TP
